@startuml state-rsvp-refined
title RSVP Lifecycle — State Machine (Refined, per createRsvp / approveRsvp / rejectRsvp)

state "Choice: admission & approval" as C <<choice>>

[*] --> Validating : POST /api/events/:id/rsvp

Validating --> Blocked : accepting_rsvp = false\n/ own event / duplicate RSVP\n/ time conflict / travel risk\n/ capacity reached
Validating --> C : checks pass

C --> Confirmed : [mode=capacity && require_approval=false]\n approved=true, pending=false\n (creates event_members row)
C --> CandidateList : [mode=waitlist]\n pending=true  (organizer/algorithm reviews)
C --> PendingApproval : [mode=capacity && require_approval=true]\n pending=true

state PendingApproval {
  [*] --> AwaitingOwner
}

PendingApproval --> Confirmed : approveRsvp()\n approved=true, pending=false,\n membership_id set
PendingApproval --> Rejected : rejectRsvp()\n row + membership deleted

CandidateList --> Confirmed : approveRsvp()
CandidateList --> Rejected : rejectRsvp()

Confirmed --> CheckedIn : selfCheckIn() / markAttendance()\n (method = self | manual)

Blocked --> [*] : 4xx returned, no RSVP row
Rejected --> [*] : notification RSVP_REJECTED sent
CheckedIn --> [*]

note right of Confirmed
  Persisted as rsvps row:
  approved=true, rejected=false, pending=false.
  Owner notified (type=RSVP / RSVP_APPROVED).
end note

note bottom of CheckedIn
  Separate `attendance` row
  (checked_in, check_in_method, checked_in_at).
  Requires an approved RSVP.
end note
@enduml
